    "title": "T4: the admin's older pages on the table standard; sorting inside sections; capped lists say \"400+\"",
    "why": "design/table-standard.md, T3-T5 (Jason: \"go on all three\"; T4 approved 2026-11-19). The table standard for tables the server writes moves, whole, into js/tv-table.js and app/ui/table-kit.php so the admin's older pages (in a frame, without the admin kit) get it: Insights (4 lists), Sources (3), Missed searches (2), Published, a content template's Versions and a guide's names. A table with no <thead> reads its first row of headings as its head; a link to one row opens its page. Sorting a list with sections (the Control Board's) used to move nothing; now rows sort inside each section, sections follow on Process and Status (worst first), and a closed section says \"sorted by Stage\" (Jason: \"Say 'sorted by Stage'\"). A capped tool's list says \"of 400+\" with a line to search or filter. Nothing dropped: every link, button, inline form, row colour and phone label is kept. FAQ.",
